event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","item_id":"rs_0ce1aad33941b19f016aca50139a6887d19279d58e19726dcc","output_index":0,"sequence_number":92,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Considering server rendering implementation**\n\nI'm thinking about implementing server-rendered forms without needing JavaScript. I need to ensure there's accessible input validation with alerts and proper navigation through redirects. Using SQLite will help with synchronous IDs and autoincrement features. I should set up tests using Node to spawn a local database while ignoring temp data with mkdtemp for cleanup. Finally, I want to focus on HTTP tests and persistence, but it's worth noting there won't be browser tests involved."}

